--[[
The Engine of the Tide, compact: the great machine under the palace, where the tide once turned the wheel that made the
lightning of the city, before the wheel was made to drink the tide. Dark, hot and loud.

The sluice to the heart of the Engine opens when its wheel turns counterclockwise. The train of cogs from the drive:
the five pegs of the straight row make it turn the wrong way. The shaft below (two cogs on one rod, across a pit: they
turn the same way) flips the turn, but the second motor next to it jams the train while it runs: its breaker is in the
deep gallery, only reached through the duct (the vent in the hall of the wheel). Loose cogs: two in the store behind the
pulsing plates (west), one on the ledge across the void (east, the grapnel), one in the deep gallery, one on the
conveyor of the south hall.
]]
